  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"NEWS is made up of the front pages of 100 newspapers from far-flung lands. They were collected during calendar year 2010 and reworked by the artist."--Verso of title page.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The present inundates us with headlines, which then fade quickly. The artist draws our attention to this phenomenon by causing the front pages of one hundred newspapers to become overgrown with vegetation, creating a metaphor for the nullity of the moment in the great clockwork of nature."--Publisher's description.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">For the project "News", Swiss artist Thomas Flechtner collected newspaper front pages, scattered plant seeds over them, watered them, and exposed them to the sun. The publication shows the artist's reflection on time and memory and the fleetingness of world news in a portfolio of 108 printed-on newspaper pages.</subfield>
  </datafield>
